<p>Pope Leo traveled to Monaco on Saturday for the first western European trip of his papacy, choosing one of the world’s wealthiest and smallest states for a one-day visit that surprised many Vatican observers. The US-born pontiff, described in the coverage as a former missionary with a pro-poor message, was due to arrive by helicopter, meet Prince Albert II and Princess Charlene, and begin the visit at the Prince’s Palace before later meeting youth and catechumens and celebrating Mass at Stade Louis-II. The visit stands out both for its symbolism and its rarity. Monaco is widely known for casinos, luxury yachts and concentrated wealth, but it is also a deeply Catholic principality, giving Leo a striking setting for an early message about social priorities and the place of the church in affluent societies. It is the first papal visit to Monaco since 1538, adding unusual historical weight to the trip.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/Jrk7ByixUh0PHTOnDQ2NFzS8LE17pqKiYQWJ9suVhFEjm5KjMoIlQagrgYAx94m46Ts-0qmDRRnoSnhuLZJwtsaGmDHERSIq8D8R9b93zhnDmDhzaMS22zu3p5QiRoWYc82m16JZBqtr-aK1gCGZdjrILu1K-PX6QqvtmbGvMpvF_ah3GKT9zUWviPIkMFj2XfMSaXC96JFm0ghYuJCIb8W61x7VQ2BFWUZIXDIYWb066mxWdWSsy_w' alt='Pope Leo XIV at the Vatican, March 25, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Royal welcome: Prince Albert II and Princess Charlene were expected to greet Leo at Monaco’s heliport before accompanying him into the principality’s official program.</li><li>Unexpected choice: Le Monde reported that the trip surprised not only outside observers but also French bishops, underlining how unusual Monaco was as the pope’s first stop in western Europe.</li><li>Catholic setting: The Guardian described Monaco as small, wealthy and very Catholic, helping explain why the Vatican may see the principality as both symbolically rich and pastorally relevant.</li><li>Public visibility: In Monte Carlo, billboards showing Leo were already on display ahead of the visit, signaling a prominent local effort to mark the day.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Pope Leo: His choice of Monaco for an early European trip, paired with reporting that he has been critical of wealthy elites and carries a pro-poor message, suggests he is bringing social priorities directly into one of Europe’s richest settings. (<a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/europe/article/3348236/pope-leo-heads-swanky-monaco-pro-poor-message'>South China Morning Post</a>)</li><li>Vatican observers: Some observers expressed bemusement at Monaco being selected for the first European trip of the papacy, especially given the long gap since the last papal visit. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/mar/28/pope-leo-monaco-papal-visit'>The Guardian</a>)</li><li>Monaco authorities: The visit program centered on the palace, youth encounters and a public Mass. (<a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/france/article/2026/03/28/behind-the-scenes-of-the-pope-s-unexpected-visit-to-monaco_6751889_7.html'>Le Monde</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/europe/article/3348236/pope-leo-heads-swanky-monaco-pro-poor-message'>Pope Leo heads to swanky Monaco with pro-poor message</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/pope-brings-pro-poor-message-to-swanky-monaco'>Pope brings pro-poor message to swanky Monaco</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/france/article/2026/03/28/behind-the-scenes-of-the-pope-s-unexpected-visit-to-monaco_6751889_7.html'>Behind the scenes of the pope&#x27;s unexpected visit to Monaco</a> - lemonde.fr</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/mar/28/pope-leo-monaco-papal-visit'>Pope Leo heads to Monaco 488 years after the last papal visit</a> - theguardian.com</li></ul>